-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let a sequence of lists satisfy $L_0=[\,]$ and $L_{n+1}=L_n\,E_n$ (append $E_n$).
--
--   1. **Length.** $|L_n|=\sum_{i<n}|E_i|$.
--   2. **Prefixes.** For $i\le j$, $L_i$ is an initial segment of $L_j$:
--   $$
--   L_i\ \text{is a prefix of}\ L_j ,
--   $$
--   so every entry keeps its original index forever.
